<Slide notes={`Three trials, mean and standard deviation, the same 199 questions. Overall 30.39 plus or minus 1.25 against the paper's per-category numbers — the paper does not report an overall column, which is itself worth noticing, because the average hides the disagreement. Single-hop is 44.00 against 27.02, seventeen points stronger; temporal 20.17 against 12.14. DeepSeek is simply the better reader there. Open-domain collapses to 10.25 against 44.65 — DeepSeek answers 'not mentioned' and category three punishes exactly that. And multi-hop, the category the whole thesis rests on, is 27.39 against 45.85 — that number did not transfer. Note the standard deviation: 3.48, ten times the spread of single-hop.`} style={{ padding: 0, background: '#FFFFFF', fontFamily: 'Arial' }}>
